ue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/109061","id":3134619014,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc661n2G","user":{"login":"raulsntos","id":3903059,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM5MDMwNTk=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3903059?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/raulsntos","html_url":"https://github.com/raulsntos","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/raulsntos/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/raulsntos/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/raulsntos/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/raulsntos/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/raulsntos/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/raulsntos/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/raulsntos/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/raulsntos/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/raulsntos/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-07-30T01:59:14Z","updated_at":"2025-07-30T01:59:14Z","body":"@MattParkerDev is correct. C# source generators can't consume the output of other source generators, so the Godot source generators won't be able to generate the code to register the methods that are generated by other source generators.\n\n@Ryhon0 as you found out, you can define a partial method in your source code like you do with `GeneratedMethod2` in your MRP.\n\n- To keep the conversation in one place, I'll close this issue since it's a duplicate of https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/66597","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3134619014/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]